      "line": 160,
      "title": "Reconcile current mint phase with its pinned observation timestamp",
      "evidence": "The gate accepts any integer0..3 current_phase; it does not derive the expected phase from chain.observed_block.timestamp and the configured inclusive phase windows. The helper implements that deterministic calculation at src/ZZZSeaDropMint.sol:230-237.",
      "effect": "An internally contradictory offline observation (TEAM during PUBLIC, or PUBLIC after the end) can pass this portion of mint inventory consistency. The ordinary observer reads the real getter; this is a consistency/diagnostic gap, not authority to bypass contract phase checks or proof of a live exploit.",
      "minimal_fix": "Derive expected phase from the already pinned timestamp and reviewed disjoint windows. Require exact equality, retaining0 before/after sale and between phases; do not require sale to be open for release review. Component fixtures need a matching pinned timestamp and focused inclusive-boundary/gap/mismatch cases.",
      "resolution": "fixed locally after the pinned read-only review; see fix_verification"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONSUMER-02",
      "priority": "P3",
      "file": "zzz_ops/production_v15.py",
      "line": 167,
      "title": "Reject boolean aliases for empty disabled mint-family counters",
      "evidence": "The chained comparison signer_count==token_gate_count==0 accepts Python False as0, unlike the nearby exact-type current_phase and mint-count checks.",
      "effect": "A malformed manually supplied observation can pass those empty-family fields. The actual observer produces integer lengths, so this is strict offline-format validation, not an onchain permission bypass.",
      "minimal_fix": "Require type(value)is int and value==0 for each count; retain existing actual zero-family requirement.",
      "resolution": "fixed locally after the pinned read-only review; see fix_verification"
    }
